Chamfers: the pieces of the parts that patch 0531 cuts a chamfer into
are generated by the spine's edges they run along (mitcad#1341).

0531 computes a chamfer wider than a narrow face beside its edges again
with that face unbounded and cuts it by the faces beyond into parts, the
first the stripe's and the others new stripes. The pieces cut at the
crossings are new surface data, and in the later parts every piece has a
surface of its own; the map of the spine's edges to the surfaces they
generate (myEVIMap, read by Generated) held only the surfaces computed
before the cut. Generated left out half of a fin's top chamfer faces (five
of ten), which a caller naming faces by the edges that generate them could
not name. Every piece of every part is now mapped to the spine's edges
whose parameter range it overlaps.

Test: geometry/tests/test_fillet_fin_top_creases.cpp, a reported fin's top
chamfered over side strips narrower than the chamfer: every chamfer face is
generated by a contour edge (five of ten without the patch).

Upstream: new.

